name o4-03-energy-split-1
timeout 600

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 3 OF 10 — the head-on geometry of sortie 1 with 6,000 m and 100 kt handed to the
# MiG. doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md mission 3. The mirror (the F-16 high) is
# doc/duels.md row 3 `duel-viper-high` and is NOT re-flown here; its number is quoted below.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: energy is worth more to the side whose round is fire-and-forget — is it?
# MEASURED in doc/duels.md rows 3 and 4, both draws: from 6,000 m up the MiG's Rtr goes 10.25 -> 15.12 nm
# and its Raero 39.2 -> 55.7, so it shoots FIRST and gets three rounds away while the F-16 never fires;
# with the energy on the F-16 its own Rtr goes 9.78 -> 10.84 and the AIM-120 arrives 4.57 m out instead
# of 7.52. Height buys the MiG a longer shot it must then ILLUMINATE to impact, and it buys the F-16 a
# closer arrival it owes nothing for. Same 6,000 m, two different currencies.
#
# AND THIS IS WHERE THE CAMPAIGN'S CARRY BITES, deliberately. Sorties 1 and 2 were flown by these same
# two airframes and the campaign carries `stores`. Four AIM-120 and two R-27R went out on the range
# period's first two sorties; whatever is left is what flies here, and the `set store` lines below that
# the book cannot cover are DROPPED before the spawn (`campaign CARRY` in this step's events.log).
# The F-16's BVR advantage in this tree is a magazine as much as a radar, and a magazine is the one thing
# a sequence of sorties can take away. Compare this step's run against its own standalone run — both are
# in the campaign report, and the difference between them is the entire content of the campaign layer.
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-29), and this is the campaign's own headline. Both runs exit 3 and they draw for
# OPPOSITE reasons:
#   STANDALONE  the MiG holds the energy and owns the fight: it releases at t=147.4 and t=393.1, its
#               R-27R arrives 10.16 m out, and the F-16 NEVER FIRES (doc/duels.md row 4 reproduced).
#   IN CAMPAIGN sorties 1 and 2 have taken three AIM-120 off the F-16 and BOTH R-27R off the MiG (five
#               `campaign CARRY` lines). The MiG now launches an R-73 at 16,713 m — a heat-seeker at
#               nine miles, which never arrives — and the F-16, which fired nothing standalone, puts its
#               last AMRAAM 5.13 m from the MiG and follows with an AIM-9.
# The engagement INVERTS. The F-16's BVR advantage in this tree is a magazine as much as a radar, and a
# magazine is exactly what a sequence of sorties can take away.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 (TIMEOUT) standalone. In the campaign the exit code is whatever the remaining
# rounds allow, and it is a RESULT and not a defect. Read, in this order: the `campaign CARRY` lines,
# then eng_shot_s / eng_shot_nm / eng_shot_rtr_nm on both sides, then the DETONATION lines. exit 2 would
# be a defect.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 12.72600 6000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode crm
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set rwr on
  set store 1 aim120
  set store 2 aim120
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 4 aim120
  set store 6 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 6000 400
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.20000 14.47400 12000 270.0 500     # 6,000 m and 100 kt in hand
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_mode rad
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set store 1 r73
  set store 2 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  # THE CONTROLLER HAS TO SAY THE ANGELS, and on this geometry it is not a nicety but the asymmetry
  # itself. The N019's search bar is +-6 deg in elevation against the APG-68's +-10.5, and the intercept's
  # Search state aims the antenna at the BRIEFED band — without a call that is this jet's own altitude.
  # [MESS] the first cut of this file omitted the line: 6,000 m of separation put the F-16 outside the
  # bar at gate range and the MiG searched its own level for the whole run, eng_detect_s = -1, not one
  # contact, and the F-16 killed it at 1.43 m without ever being seen. The F-16 in the mirror geometry
  # needs no equivalent. Same mechanism, same numbers as duel-fulcrum-high.fbm.
  set brief_gci 20 270 99 6
  set task intercept
  wp 55.20000 12.60000 12000 500
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive

unit hulkwest
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 55.20000 12.60000 ground 90.0 0

unit hulkeast
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 55.20000 14.60000 ground 270.0 0
